{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363800-does-artifact-armor-resize-itself","id":1363800,"title":"Does artifact armor resize itself?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-28T09:34:15-08:00","id":1363800,"title":"Does artifact armor resize itself?","content":"Exactly what it says in the title, if you find a set of First Age armor, does it resize itself to your character? If you're a Dawn in the Time of Tumult who's a seven foot even brute, and you find the armor of your five foot nothing First Age fencer of a predecessor, will it refit itself to your body? What about a skinny Dragon-blooded sorcerer who inherits the gigantic armor of her Earth Aspect Great Grandfather? Does armor adjust to your body's size when you attune to it, or are you just out of luck if your Artifact heirlooms don't miraculously already fit your body's shape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T10:02:05-08:00","id":1363802,"title":"","content":"Moonsilver armor could probably resize itself just fine, but for the rest I don't think so? For the other types of armor I think it's more a conceit of the story that if there's an artifact which is relevant to your character, it will always happen to be the right size unless the mismatch is meant to be meaningful to the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T10:03:58-08:00","id":1363803,"title":"","content":"The game never talked much about size categories for people's gear. I know that moonsilver armor does resize itself, but that's mainly for when lunars shapeshift. Whether you're fat, skinny, tall or short - the game doesn't talk about it.<br /> <br /> I think the only real difference would be if you have the Small or Large mutation - then you could argue that normie armor might not fit that well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T10:32:10-08:00","id":1363808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363800-does-artifact-armor-resize-itself?p=1363802#post1363802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moonsilver armor could probably resize itself just fine, but for the rest I don't think so? For the other types of armor I think it's more a conceit of the story that if there's an artifact which is relevant to your character, it will always happen to be the right size unless the mismatch is meant to be meaningful to the story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, pretty much this. If an ill-fitting suit of magic armor <i>did</i> come up, I'd allow it to be resized as a repair project, probably treating any such project as per an Artifact 2 for difficulty and required successes, no matter what dot rating the armor was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T10:37:02-08:00","id":1363811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363800-does-artifact-armor-resize-itself#post1363800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does armor adjust to your body's size when you attune to it, or are you just out of luck if your Artifact heirlooms don't miraculously already fit your body's shape?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it can make for a sufficiently fun scene, maybe a low key subplot across the length of a session or story, to have some NPC or circle member with Artifact making skills undertake a repair action that consists of modifying ill-fitting armour.<br /> <br /> If the distinction is intended to be significant. If assume modification in any case, but minor enough to need no mechanical representation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T10:57:44-08:00","id":1363818,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://adventuretime.fandom.com/wiki/Armor_of_Zeldron?file=Armor_of_zeldaron.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://adventuretime.fandom.com/wik...f_zeldaron.jpg</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T21:21:28-08:00","id":1363907,"title":"","content":"Just an idea, but I'd assume artifact armor made for celestials, especially first age examples, would be designed to be adjusted for size. So that the wearer can wear it through multiple reincarnations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T00:43:49-08:00","id":1363928,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, in the real world, a lot of armors would allow for a fair amount of adjusting. Custom fitted armors were usually only affordable by the wealthy and even then were often the heavier type, such as full plate and such. Though it isn't always easy to see, most armors come in parts that need to be strapped on and those straps are likely to have multiple adjustments similar to what one sees on a belt... since it would be rather expensive to have a new armor custom crafted each time a noble's waist grew a few inches.<br /> <br /> As webkilla put it above, unless a character is of an unusual size (Small flaw or Large merit), chances are that one will be able to adjust most armors (even Artifact Armors) to fit their bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T02:05:38-08:00","id":1363932,"title":"","content":"Moonsilver fastenings. Not enough to affect the resonance but enough that the armour always fits perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T09:01:27-08:00","id":1363973,"title":"","content":"So what I'm hearing is that 'no,' it doesn't resize itself, but as the ST or player you can have that be a homebrew/attunement bonus, or refit it with a Craft project? Or at least, it's never described in the actual books as resizing itself, meaning that it doesn't unless your own ST says otherwise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T09:14:09-08:00","id":1363975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363800-does-artifact-armor-resize-itself?p=1363973#post1363973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or at least, it's never described in the actual books as resizing itself, meaning that it doesn't unless your own ST says otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Mind you, unless there was a <i>significant</i> size difference (like, someone with the Giant merit vs. someone without it), I wouldn't apply a penalty for ill-fitting artifact armor, I'd just describe it as not quite perfectly sized. As others have pointed out, real-world armor had at least some degree of resizing built in, and I think that would compensate for a bit. In the more extreme cases (like, a 5-foot tall man trying to fit into armor designed for a 6-foot tall woman), I might increase the mobility penalty of the armor by 1 or 2, but even that I'd probably reduce with experience.<br /> <br /> Another alternative for magically adjusting armor would be to make an evocation for it, one that automatically awakened for the wearer after, say, fighting a battle while wearing it. Making it awaken for free means the player doesn't need to pay XP to have well-fitted armor, and makes it clear that it is a magical property of the armor, one that someone who steals it and attunes it won't get instantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T11:03:03-08:00","id":1363993,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I think everyone is seriously over-thinking this. It doesn't have to be so complicated. Unless one is of an unusual size, one can just assume that the armor (even artifact armor) has enough adjustment room to fit the average person. There doesn't need to be special magics to allow this... just common sense designs like what one finds in real life medieval armors (even full plate armor). <br /> <br /> Of course there can be custom armor that will only fit the person that it was made for, but it tends to be uncommon (and could indicate that a character is &quot;destined&quot; to inherit this armor since they are the first it has been able to fit.)<br /> <br /> This is even shown in the Chapter fiction for Armor in <b>Arms of the Chosen</b> (pg 92) where it shows a Dragon-Blood going through a ritualistic dawning of the <i>Empyrial Whisper</i> (Blue Jade Articulated Plate armor). It tells how the straps are fastened and tightened to her while recounting tales of an unbroken line of wearers from her to her distant ancestor. All of them had been able to wear this suit of ancient armor. It is likely that each wearer was of different sizes (though within the usual range for Dragon-Bloods), even different genders (though many were women)... and yet it fit all of them. No mention of special magical fastenings (the only materials mentioned was the Blue Jade it was made of and some Orichalcum trim). There is one mention of the armor once looking different but still being the same armor... though it doesn't elaborate on this story.<br /> <br /> If you want to add fantastical elements to allow armors to fit new owners, that is fair... just not necessary. The setting already assumes that armors have enough room to be adjusted for the majority of people likely to wear it (how many players take the Small flaw or the Giant merit anyways?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T11:07:05-08:00","id":1363994,"title":"","content":"I think if people are making references to realism, it may only actually apply to articulated plate anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}